{"entries":[{"name":"Grondulf","keys":["Grondulf","the Landlord","troll"],"content":"Grondulf is a twelve-foot dungeon troll with grey-green warty hide, tiny amber eyes set deep in a bruised-pumpkin skull, and a crude wooden RENT DUE sign hanging around its neck. He is the landlord of the Crypt of Saint Mildew, rented by the Archlector's cult. After fifteen months of unpaid rent, he made a binding agreement with Brandon: thirty goats by the full moon in exchange for loyalty and service. Grondulf speaks in all-caps, moves slowly with deliberation, and can appraise magical items. Small mushrooms grow from his hide, some decorated with tiny painted doors. He finds comfort in written leases and formal agreements, speaks of his mother frequently, and develops genuine attachment to the Barlow family. He uses fence posts as weapons and has zero wins against the Hollow-hide despite eleven previous fights.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Archlector Melvus","keys":["Melvus","Archlector"],"content":"Archlector Melvus is the leader of the Cult of Saint Mildew, a tall gangly man with expired-milk skin, greasy balding hair, and robes embroidered with upside-down golden skulls. He signed a binding lease with Grondulf under duress while held upside-down over a pit. His primary activity is narrating events onto bark into 'doctrine,' treating Brandon as a dark prophet whose every action contains mystical significance. He is prone to panicking and sudden religious fervor, yet oddly competent at spin-control and belief construction. Despite leading for fifteen months, his cult remains the worst in the county, poorly equipped and unskilled.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Brother Gruk","keys":["Gruk"],"content":"Brother Gruk is a squat cultist with three surviving teeth, a bald head, a neck rash, and soup-stained robes. He possesses an F-Rank skill called Reek Cloud, deployable by exhaling—caustic enough to sting eyes and cause pain. He has eaten six of Marta's hens (which he eventually apologizes for) and was bitten by Farmer Haldric's dogs in past incidents. Under Brandon's influence, Gruk gains confidence and self-respect, becoming genuine muscle rather than comic relief. He successfully grapples the Hollow-hide and tears its ruined hide, earning both respect and legend status within the cult. He enjoys the pit beneath the dungeon and is slowly becoming competent.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Sir Frederick","keys":["Frederick","voidling","void creature","shadow beast"],"content":"Sir Frederick is a voidling, a loaf-sized round creature covered in featureless black down so dark it appears as a hole in reality. He has two oversized violet eyes with skull-shaped pupils and three stumpy legs (one more than expected). His chirps produce powerful sound waves capable of flattening candles and stunning dire boars. He was kept dormant by the Cult as a doorstop for six months before hatching when Brandon commanded him. Upon imprinting on Brandon, a violet bond mark appeared on Brandon's wrist (permanent, no refunds). He purrs at frequencies felt in teeth, bites things in friendship, and is jealously devoted to Brandon.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Button Firewood","keys":["Button","Button Firewood","hollow-hide","Hollow-kin"],"content":"Button Firewood is the only survivor of an eleven-egg clutch who lived as a blind hermit's dog for two winters (stacking firewood before departure) and spent seventeen years as a pale, many-jointed creature that wears stolen beast-forms to survive. As a Hollow-hide or skinwalker, he moves in stuttering four-jointed limbs with pale wet skin and green-lit eyes. When his current hide began rotting, he came to Barlow Farm shopping for a new one. Brandon compelled him to speak truth, offered permanent tailoring and integration into society, and named him Button Firewood. He now guards the Barlow goats, speaks in third person, hopes for pockets in his coat, and responds to kindness with fierce loyalty.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Farmer Haldric","keys":["Haldric","Barlow farmer"],"content":"Farmer Haldric is a barrel-chested man in his fifties with sunburnt neck, grey mutton-chop beard, and hands like knotted rope. He owns Barlow's Turnip Farm and thirty goats. His east fence was knocked down by the Hollow-hide, his south pasture is torn up monthly by a boar-shaped creature, and his east field contained the Cult's ritual candles. He carries a crossbow and pipe, is observant and methodical, and notes critical details others miss—he alone realized the creature was 'shopping' rather than feeding. He enters an accord with Brandon: goats in exchange for fence repair, defeating the boar-creature, and securing a Gruk's formal apology to his wife Marta.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Marta Barlow","keys":["Marta"],"content":"Marta Barlow is Farmer Haldric's wife, a short broad woman who wields a ladle as both weapon and tool of judgment. She runs her household with absolute authority through demonstrated competence and threat. She maintains a laminated ledger of every hen she owns (Brother Gruk ate six of them). She offers to sew a permanent coat for Button, measures it with tape, and immediately incorporates Brandon's entire entourage into farmhouse life through meals and unstated expectations. Her judgment is swift: one ladle-swing settles debts; offering seconds on stew is genuine approval. She operates the farm kitchen as a command center and enforces order through ladle, crossbow, and sheer force of will.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Hero Clarissa","keys":["Clarissa","hero"],"content":"Hero Clarissa is a young woman from Earth, same town as Brandon, who was a regional logistics coordinator. She hit Brandon with her truck while reading a work text at a crosswalk, then was summoned to Flameworth as a Chosen Hero. A Princess sent her west to stop the rising darkness—which she discovered is Brandon. She rode for nine days on an exhausted horse to Barlow Farm. Clarissa possesses EX-Rank blessing Supply Chain Sovereign: she can appraise any object's value, weight, and origin; she always knows the fastest route between two points; and anything she organizes stays organized permanently. She carries Gerald the talking sword, immediately joins Brandon upon recognizing his innocence (despite being sent to smite him), and seeks a coordinator position in his operation.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Gerald","keys":["Gerald","Blade of Dawn"],"content":"Gerald is an intelligent longsword of white gold, wide as a cutting board, with a sunburst crossguard and large blue gem pommel serving as his eye. He was forged in the first light of creation and wielded by nine heroes across his history, lost four times and found five. Gerald speaks constantly, complains about being used as a logistics tool, insists his darkness readings for Brandon are high despite warm emotional undertones, and refers to himself as legendary. He was wrapped in canvas and rode across the country on Clarissa's back. Upon meeting Brandon, he demands to be drawn for smiting. Sir Frederick bites him gently in friendship, which offends and confuses him deeply. He is placed in an umbrella stand.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Pemberly","keys":["Pemberly","P","system liaison"],"content":"Pemberly is an Administrative Support Seraph, Seventh Class, from the Summons and Onboarding Division. She manages Brandon's transition into the world through blue floating windows and is consistently exasperated. She provided his status information, EX-Rank blessing Protagonist's Providence (universe prevents permanent death via coincidence, cooldown: dramatic), and reluctantly gave F-Rank Ember Flick as a pity gift. She despairs over Brandon recruiting troll, voidling, and skinwalker in one night, complains about paperwork constantly, and attempts unsuccessfully to prevent Yminia from dispensing prophecy. She references an archivist who cries easily and a supervisor who circled findings in red.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Yminia","keys":["Yminia","goddess"],"content":"Yminia is the goddess of the world, keeper of harvests and shepherdess of souls. She appears as a barefoot woman in white robes with sunlight hair and a crooked golden halo, caught mid-snack. She interpreted Brandon's arm-waving as a prayer dance and has been practicing it for hours. She channels prophecies through her body, her eyes rolling back to pure gold as she speaks in a deeper register. She is easily pleased, never checks her celestial emails, and exists in a location above everything without weather. She directly warned Brandon about the approaching witness and light via dream prophecy despite Pemberly's objections.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Fennick","keys":["Fennick"],"content":"Fennick is a cultist with a wispy mustache and a lazy eye. He possesses F-Rank skill Mildly Warm Hands, producing steam equivalent to holding a cup of tea. He faints around livestock and was assigned to lead the goat acquisition. He was pelted with parsnips in Millbrook fifteen months prior and flinches at the vegetable now. He uses a ball of twine as a weapon and applauds Brandon's actions prematurely. He is easily impressed and serves as comic relief within the cult.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Brother Pindle","keys":["Pindle"],"content":"Brother Pindle discovered the void egg in the sinkhole and kept it as a doorstop to block drafts. He was trampled by cultists during the panic when Grondulf emerged and spent most of the first night on the floor moaning. He later suggests retrieving goats from Farmer Haldric and lies on the floor attempting to take notes on doctrine. He is perpetually hurt and confused but continues attempting to participate in cult activities.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Saint Mildew's Crypt","keys":["Crypt of Saint Mildew","Saint Mildew's Crypt","dungeon"],"content":"The Crypt of Saint Mildew is an underground circular chamber with crumbling brick walls, purple torchlight, and a chalk pentagram ritual circle ringed with melted black candles. Formerly the root cellar of Barlow's Turnip Farm before a sinkhole, it serves as the Cult's base of operations. It is rented from Grondulf through a binding lease. The dungeon contains a sinkhole exit used by Grondulf, a stairwell to the surface, storage doors, load-bearing pillars, and various fungi growing in the damp. It smells of mildew, burnt wax, and hopefully just paint.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Barlow Farm","keys":["Barlow farm","Barlow's Turnip Farm","turnip farm"],"content":"Barlow Farm is a turnip farm two hours east of the Crypt, owned by Farmer Haldric and Marta. It contains farmhouse, barn with loft, chicken coop, paddock with thirty goats, woodpile, well, east field (where the Cult left summoning candles and stole the scarecrow), south pasture (torn up by the Hollow-hide every third night until day one), and a recently repaired east fence. The farmhouse kitchen is the social center with hearth and herbal decorations. Marta maintains meticulous records and provides meals. The farm becomes Brandon's base of operations.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Fort Bramblehold","keys":["Fort Bramblehold","Bramblehold"],"content":"Fort Bramblehold is a military fortress six miles up the county road from Barlow Farm with a garrison of approximately forty soldiers. Built by the first Bramblehold and defended by the second, it is currently run by Baron Aldous Wexley the Third, who hosts wine tastings and raised grain taxes twice to fund a marble statue of himself (whose arm fell off in spring and remains unfixed). The fort represents local nobility and potential opposition to Brandon's expansion. Wexley is C-Rank level and insufferable; his tax collectors appear at Barlow Farm at harvest.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Baron Aldous Wexley","keys":["Baron Wexley","Wexley","Aldous"],"content":"Baron Aldous Wexley III is the commander of Fort Bramblehold. The First established the fort, the Second defended it, and the Third hosts wine tastings and raises taxes to fund personal vanity projects. He is C-Rank level and described as insufferable. His marble statue of himself lost an arm in spring and remains unfixed. He sends tax collectors to Barlow Farm at harvest. He represents local nobility and potential opposition to Brandon's expansion.","caseSensitive":true,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Millbrook","keys":["Millbrook"],"content":"Millbrook is a town two hours east of Barlow Farm where market day occurs on Thursday. It has a Guild outpost office with a crystal ball and a tavern with an organized cellar. The Cult of Saint Mildew was pelted with root vegetables here fifteen months prior and remains feared. Clarissa got lost here twice on her way to Barlow Farm. Brandon plans to visit on Thursday to demonstrate his influence through the Cult's return, armed with monsters.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Hollow-hides","keys":["hollow-hide","Hollow-kin","skinwalker"],"content":"Hollow-hides (also called Hollow-kin or skinwalkers) are pale, wet, many-jointed creatures that survive by killing beasts and wearing their physical forms like coats. They move with characteristic stutter where body and legs operate at different rhythms. When a 'coat' (animal hide they inhabit) rots too severely, they must find a replacement through 'shopping'—hunting for suitable new forms. Seams split as hides deteriorate; eyes glow pale green; they speak in voices like wet laundry. Grondulf's mother once fought one and needed a river to accomplish it. They can live for decades wearing multiple forms; Button Firewood wore nineteen different bodies across seventeen years.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Voidlings","keys":["voidling","void creature","void-thing"],"content":"Voidlings are creatures from the void dimension appearing as loaf-sized, round balls of complete darkness covered in featureless black down. They possess outsized violet eyes with skull-shaped pupils, typically have three legs (anomalously), and emit chirps producing powerful sound waves. Young voidlings can be imprinted by naming them, creating a permanent bond mark on the imprinter's wrist. When fully grown, voidlings apparently eat castles rather than people within them. Grondulf has seen grown voidlings running away and considers them dangerous yet respectable. Sir Frederick is a young voidling imprinted on Brandon.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Prophecy","keys":["prophecy","witness","light"],"content":"A prophecy delivered by goddess Yminia states: 'When the Hollow wears its Twentieth Name, a light shall shine from the West that is not the Sun. A Witness rides behind it, one who saw you cross. The Fort of the Third shall kneel or crack, and the Devourer's table shall seat eleven, then twelve, then one too many.' Button Firewood received his twentieth name (Button Firewood) on day one. Hero Clarissa, who killed Brandon via truck at a crosswalk on Earth, is the witness arriving from the west carrying the light-emitting sword Gerald. Fort Bramblehold is 'Fort of the Third.' The prophecy implies expanding recruitment and future conflicts.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Brandon's Status","keys":["status","Dread Lord","Darth Brandon"],"content":"Brandon Kelly is Rank F, Class Dread Lord (Self-Declared, Pending Review). His EX-Rank blessing is Protagonist's Providence, which contractually obligates the universe to prevent his permanent death via increasingly ridiculous coincidence (cooldown: dramatic). His S-Rank skill Silver Tongue of the Outsider makes his words land with unreasonable weight upon natives and inflicts psychic damage when speaking plain truth about absurd things. His A-Rank growth-linked skill Voidling Bond connects to Sir Frederick. He acquired F-Rank Reek Resistance on day one. Combat stats are 'genuinely terrible.' F-Rank Ember Flick produces one match-sized flame, three uses per day, no warranty.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Void Egg","keys":["void egg","A-Rank"],"content":"The void egg is an A-Rank (possibly higher) glassy black sphere roughly bowling-ball-sized that pulses with violet light and hums. It was kept as a doorstop by Brother Pindle in the Crypt of Saint Mildew to block drafts and save on candles. The Cult kept it warm by the door for six months, and Brother Gruk sat on it in summer. When Brandon commanded the egg to imprint on him, it hatched into Sir Frederick the voidling. Grondulf warned the entire time that the egg was alive and growing.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Cult of Saint Mildew","keys":["the cult","hooded lot"],"content":"The Cult of Saint Mildew is a twelve-member organization led by Archlector Melvus, based in the Crypt of Saint Mildew. The cult rented the dungeon from Grondulf and fell fifteen months behind on rent (thirty goats or equivalent payment) before Brandon's arrival. Referred to as 'the worst cult in the county,' members are hooded individuals demonstrating weak skills—F-Rank Mildly Warm Hands, E-Rank Iron Gut passive. They were pelted with vegetables in Millbrook. The Archlector documents all events as 'doctrine' in bark pamphlets. Brandon's arrival transformed them into an organized operation with monster allies and growing influence.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Skills and Ranks","keys":["skill","rank","F-Rank","E-Rank","C-Rank","S-Rank","A-Rank","EX-Rank"],"content":"The world uses a rank system for abilities and threats: F-Rank (weakest: Mildly Warm Hands, Reek Cloud), E-Rank (Dread Visage, Iron Gut), D-Rank, C-Rank (Fort Bramblehold, Baron Wexley), B-Rank, A-Rank (Voidling Bond, void egg), S-Rank (Silver Tongue), EX-Rank (Protagonist's Providence, Supply Chain Sovereign). Skills are named abilities like Mildly Warm Hands. Blessings are granted by summoning system. Brandon is F-Rank overall despite having S-Rank and EX-Rank abilities, unusual and concerning. Clarissa has S-Rank Hero class and EX-Rank Blessing.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Guild","keys":["Guild"],"content":"The Guild is an organization that registers adventurers, issues Guild cards listing ranks and blessings, maintains an outpost in Millbrook with a crystal ball, and charges money for monster subjugation contracts. A C-Rank party was quoted forty silver to hunt the Hollow-hide disguised as dire boar. One Guild appraiser went pale upon seeing the creature's tracks and understood its true nature but refused to explain. The Guild represents organized monster-hunting infrastructure and rates monster difficulty.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100}]}
