{"entries":[{"name":"Gerald","keys":["Gerald","Blade of Dawn","Duskwarden"],"content":"A legendary sword forged in the first light of creation, white-gold with sunburst crossguard and blue gemstone pommel. Currently wielded by Hero Clarissa. Has been wielded by nine heroes over two centuries, but only remembers four of them. Gravely concerned that his darkness readings for Brandon are 'warm' instead of properly cold. Negotiated a consulting contract with Brandon as Duskwarden, and drafted the verse: 'The blade of dawn advised the darkness, because the dawn is nothing more than the moment the dark decides to be seen.'","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Sergeant Aldwin Crake","keys":["Crake","Aldwin","Sergeant"],"content":"Twenty-year veteran of Fort Bramblehold's garrison, gray-bearded and weathered, with one eyebrow permanently raised by an old scar. Defected alongside five other soldiers when Brandon commanded the garrison without drawing a sword, impressed by the Dread Lord's refusal to execute followers who bar gates from habit. Knows every stone of the fort, the culvert drainage route, and the fact that the garrison hadn't been paid in four months. Now leads the garrison militia for the Undergrowth.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Nessa the Miller","keys":["Nessa","miller","mill"],"content":"Tobbin's sister, runs the only working mill for eight miles in the county. Negotiated terms with the Undergrowth to grind grain at one-tenth tax rate instead of the Wexley's one-fifth levy. Demands include road repair by the mill before winter and resolution of the growing miasma pocket south of the mire that threatens her millpond. Flour-dusted and skeptical, but willing to believe in a government that returns debts and takes problems seriously.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Tobbin","keys":["Tobbin","Master of Records","clerk"],"content":"Former Millbrook clerk who copied forged levy records under duress to protect his sister Nessa's mill deed from Reeve Fenn's strongbox. Appointed Master of Records for the Undergrowth. Possesses documentation of five years of double-sealed levy frauds across three counties. Walked six miles after the Millbrook judgement to offer his records and take the position officially, promising to find the grain factor's name and every county he defrauded.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Ser Dagric Vane","keys":["Vane","Dagric","knight"],"content":"B-Rank knight sworn to Baron Wexley the Third, tourney-trained, maintains obsessively polished armor while the garrison rusts. Dueled Grondulf at the Bramblehold gates under pre-negotiated terms that he would swear fealty either way, and was relocated by the troll mid-punch like furniture. Has been secretly stealing cellar wine for years and knows the Baron's inventory better than anyone. Swore fealty to the Undergrowth with grace, and escorts removal of the crypt's contents to Dreadhold.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Undergrowth","keys":["Undergrowth","sprout","sprout banner"],"content":"The new faction established by Brandon, encompassing the cult of Saint Mildew, the Bramblehold garrison militia, recruited monsters (a troll, a voidling familiar, a hollow-hide), and allied villages and merchants. Its banner is black cloth with a single pale sprout unfurling two leaves from the bottom edge, symbolizing things that grow where nothing should. Named by the Archlector, embraced by the county.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Dreadhold","keys":["Dreadhold"],"content":"The renamed Fort Bramblehold, now serving as the capital and base of operations for the Undergrowth. Features a great hall converted to a council chamber, a courtyard flying the new sprout banner, a sour well being repaired by Grondulf, and Ser Dagric Vane's cellar as a strategic asset. Grondulf serves as property manager and has identified seven code violations needing repair before winter. Will host the representatives from eleven villages.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Grain Crisis","keys":["grain","winter","shortage","granary"],"content":"The county's winter grain reserve was mostly sold off by Reeve Fenn to eastern grain factors in August to fund the Baron's statue arm repairs. The Undergrowth must recover or purchase approximately four hundred sacks to feed the garrison, villages, and cult through winter and spring thaw, or risk starvation. Recovery is possible through Tobbin's bill of sale documentation showing fraud and the name of the grain factor with the wheat-and-weasel seal.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Miasma Pocket","keys":["miasma","mire","rot"],"content":"A growing pocket of corruption and magical rot located south of the mire, creeping slowly toward Nessa's millpond. The water at the pocket's edge has turned gray and fish float in it wrong. Nessa included resolution of this threat as a requirement of her mill agreement with the Undergrowth before spring, making it a priority problem that cannot be ignored through the winter months.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100}]}
```

