{"entries":[{"name":"Yminia","keys":["Yminia","goddess"],"content":"The four-thousand-year-old goddess of harvests, keeper of the Tapestry of Flameworth, and observer of all fate. Recently made contact with Brandon Kelly through prophetic visions to warn him of the seam-toucher entity hidden in the royal court. Established a bidirectional divine communication channel using a golden thread of her own essence. Has developed unexpected romantic and physical attraction to Brandon, complicating her usually distant divine role. Struggles with embarrassment over her own feelings and the administrative chaos her personal interest has created in the divine bureaucracy.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Miasma Pocket","keys":["sweet water","honey","sapling"],"content":"A vast consciousness that called itself the Drinker, a reality-wounded entity that fell through a hole in the Tapestry thirty years ago. Spent three decades consuming three hundred forty-one people across the county, keeping one hundred six spirits in orbit beneath its body. Brandon Kelly confronted it at the mire's heart and offered terms: the creature agreed to stop feeding in exchange for Brandon's companionship and understanding. When the Drinker attempted to reclaim consumed memories, Brandon drove a mercy-thrust into its heart-doll, and it transformed into a sapling tree with silver bark and violet-veined leaves. Now planted in Mosshaven's burned plot as a memorial and guardian, speaking in single voice for the first time in thirty years, requesting to know all visitors' names so it may remember them.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Mosshaven","keys":["Mosshaven","evacuated","refugees"],"content":"A village of twelve families in the western county, evacuated in September after poisoned wells drove them from their homes. The miasma pocket's expansion forced them to flee with nothing, and they were taken in by the miller Nessa. Upon Brandon's defeat of the Drinker, the well has become aether-blessed — the cleanest water in three counties. The families are being given permission to return. A silver sapling memorial grows on Old Yarrow's burned property, marking both his death and the Drinker's transformation. Plans include rebuilding as a waystation on the new river trade route, with the blessed well as an attraction, and the sapling tree as an eternal memorial to all three hundred forty-one of the Drinker's victims.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Brandon's Status","keys":["status","Dread Lord","Darth Brandon"],"content":"Brandon Kelly, seventeen years old, summoned to Flameworth after death-by-truck. Declared himself Dread Lord of the Undergrowth and has successfully recruited a troll landlord, a void creature, a hollow-hide, a fallen knight, a hero, and various townspeople into a de facto government. Resolved the miasma pocket crisis in three days, established a county militia, created a naval force, and is now formally invited to the royal capital by King Aurelian for Saint Halvard's coronation feast in eleven days. Currently preparing for the journey with his core companions. Possesses S-Rank Silver Tongue ability and divine connection to the goddess Yminia.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Prophecy","keys":["prophecy","witness","light"],"content":"A divine prophecy spoken by Yminia that Brandon's arrival would bring change: When the hollow wears its twentieth name, a light shall shine from the west that is not the sun. A witness rides behind it, one who saw you cross. The fort of the third shall kneel or crack, and the devourer's table shall seat eleven, then twelve, then one too many. Button Firewood became the twentieth name, the light refers to both Clarissa's arrival and the metaphorical brightness of Brandon's influence. The witness is the seam-toucher entity that observed Brandon's crossing from Earth to Flameworth — the same being embedded in the royal court for thirty years, systematically consuming Chosen Ones.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"King Aurelian","keys":["Aurelian","king","eaten"],"content":"Aurelian the First, King of Flameworth for thirty years, officially known as a Chosen One who arrived during the kingdom's founding. Secretly hollow of his own past and memories — the Drinker consumed his previous life, leaving only a puppet that the court learned to manipulate. Has grown aware that his court machinery runs without his input and no longer trusts his closest advisors. Sent a personal message to Brandon Kelly inviting him to Saint Halvard's coronation feast in his capacity as a Dread Lord. Hopes Brandon's reputation for supernatural persuasion and his void familiar will help identify the seam-toucher entity that his advisors have been hiding from him.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Seam-Toucher","keys":["seam-toucher","entity","weave"],"content":"A mysterious being existing outside the normal Tapestry of Flameworth, capable of tearing holes between the world of Earth and Flameworth. Maintains presence at the royal court for at least thirty years, systematically unpicking the Tapestry and using it as bait to summon Chosen Ones to Flameworth, then consuming them. Appeared at Brandon's crosswalk on Earth watching him be struck by a truck; thirty years earlier did the same to the golden king now known as King Aurelian; and again nineteen days ago to Clarissa. Currently embedded somewhere in the royal court with unknown identity and form, using one of the courtiers as a host. Its presence drives Brandon's invitation to the capital — King Aurelian and Yminia both hope he can identify and stop it.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Aurelium","keys":["Aurelium","city","white walls"],"content":"The capital city of Flameworth, renamed thirty years ago by King Aurelian. Features white walls with gold rooftops and appears beautiful from a distance, but internally is deeply corrupt and self-serving. The royal palace contains a summoning chamber far underground where Chosen Ones are pulled into Flameworth through holes torn by the seam-toucher. Home to half a million people and hosts the largest formal gatherings of the year. An underground faction has been quietly running the kingdom's actual business while King Aurelian was left hollow and confused on the throne. Brandon and his companions are traveling there for Saint Halvard's coronation feast.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Saint Halvard's Feast","keys":["Halvard","feast","coronation"],"content":"An annual remembrance festival held in the royal capital, celebrating a saint dead for four hundred years. The largest formal gathering of the kingdom's year, attended by every noble house, church bishops, Guild assessors, and courtiers. Despite the name, no coronation actually occurs — it is purely a commemoration and social event where the court displays its wealth and power. King Aurelian officially invited Dread Lord Brandon Kelly and his companions as honored guests in recognition of his sovereignty over the western county. The feast occurs in eleven days from Brandon's meeting with the herald. The real purpose is to place Brandon in position to identify and confront the seam-toucher entity hidden among the courtiers.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Herald Corvin Ashe","keys":["Corvin","herald","Ashe"],"content":"A Royal Herald of Third Class with twenty-two years of service to Flameworth. All heralds of his rank are bound by magical geas that forces them to deliver messages with perfect fidelity — they cannot misquote, embellish, or withhold words. This makes them invaluable for communications that cannot be corrupted. Corvin rode to the Dreadhold carrying King Aurelian's personal invitation to Brandon, delivering both official acknowledgment of the western county's sovereignty and private warning about the seam-toucher hidden in the court. Despite professional distance, showed unexpected sympathy for Brandon's position and warned that the court's actual machinery has disconnected from the king's will. Will carry Brandon's response back to the capital.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100}]}
