{"entries":[{"name":"The Seam-Toucher","keys":["seam-toucher","entity","weave"],"content":"A cosmic entity calling itself the Tailor—neither god nor woven-thing but essential staff to the loom itself. It patches the threadbare tapestry by harvesting threads from other worlds when the weave wears thin. All Summonings are its work: the seams it tears between realities to pull Chosen ones into service. Thirty years past it pulled Brandon Kelly and Hero Clarissa through one seam and mishandled the tear; the leak created the Drinker of the mire. It engineered the current King of Flameworth as its masterpiece—a perfect patch, the finest work in centuries. The Tailor operates in isolation, makes decisions with brutal triage: the unwoven are harvestable, expendable. It has been hunting an unknown third entity that operates in its own seams undetected and unseen. By agreement with the Dread Lord, it will neither protect nor hinder him further, but it watches, takes notes, and remains afraid.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Master Halloway","keys":["Halloway","honest assessor","side office"],"content":"Senior Guild assessor managing the side office at Thornwall, a man of integrity who refused to falsify records despite palace pressure. When Chancellery inspectors forced him to forge Brandon Kelly's assessment card to lower his threat rating, Halloway deliberately flawed each draft to protect the true measurement—an SS outcome rating paired with F combat stats, a discrepancy that cracked the Guild's measuring instrument. He was coerced by threat to his pension, not his person, but his character proved unbreakable. He paid out of his own purse for a courier to warn the Dread Lord, and moved the truth through back windows and bad latches rather than burned files.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"Courier Sable","keys":["Sable","courier","second class"],"content":"Guild Courier Second Class dispatched from Thornwall to deliver Brandon Kelly's sealed assessment before he reached the capital gates. She knew the Chancellery inspectors' presence, understood the implications of a forged card, and worked with the Dread Lord to rescue Master Halloway from coercion. Practical, direct, and loyal to those who prove worthy through action rather than rank. She accepted a place in the convoy to Aurelium, trading standard courier routes for something more dangerous and more real.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100},{"name":"The Unknown Witness Entity","keys":["third party","unknown watcher","the braider","corner presence"],"content":"A cosmic entity existing outside the tapestry's weave entirely, standing four feet from the Seam-Toucher itself at Brandon Kelly's intersection and invisible even to divine staff. It braided Brandon and Hero Clarissa together mid-transit through the summoning seams, binding two dead strangers into load-bearing thread without the Tailor's knowledge or permission. It has been embedded in the capital's court for thirty years, leaving no holes, making no tears, breaking no records—operating within the seams themselves where Appraisal skills cannot read it. It is feared by the Seam-Toucher but fears something itself. Its purpose remains unknown. Its motivation remains hidden. Its very existence is a wound in the cosmic record.","caseSensitive":false,"cascade":false,"throttle":100}]}
